 ],
 "literal": "If he has wealth, he is capable of eating / even beyond what is due, to those who beg, he gives / the delightful companion of simple folk, Neṭumāṉ Añci / like a fire-striking stick tucked into the eaves of a house / he is capable of remaining unseen; and then / like the intense fire that rises, spitting out sparks / he is also capable of appearing, when the time comes to appear.",
 "translation": "If he has wealth, he is capable of enjoying it with others. He gives even beyond what is due to those who come begging. Neṭumāṉ Añci, the delightful companion of simple, innocent folk, is like a fire-striking stick tucked away in the eaves of a house—capable of remaining completely unseen. But when the time comes for him to appear, he is capable of bursting forth like an intense, spark-spitting fire.",
 "modern": "செல்வம் இருந்தால் அதியமான் நெடுமான் அஞ்சி பிறருடன் பகிர்ந்து உண்ணவும் வல்லவன். கேட்பவர்களுக்குக் கடமையையும் தாண்டி வாரி வழங்குபவன். எளியவர்களின் மகிழ்ச்சியான துணைவன் அவன். வீட்டின் கூரையில் செருகி வைக்கப்பட்ட தீக்கடைக்கோல் போல வெளியே தெரியாமல் அடங்கி இருக்கவும் அவன் வல்லவன். ஆனால், அவன் வெளிப்படும் காலம் வரும்போது, நெருப்பைக் கக்கி எரியும் பெருநெருப்பைப் போலத் தோன்றவும் வல்லவன்.",
 "explanation": "This poem is composed by the famous poet Avvaiyār in praise of the chieftain Atiyamāṉ Neṭumāṉ Añci, belonging to the Vākai (victory) tiṇai and Vallāṉ Mullai tuṟai, which celebrates the strength and virtues of a powerful warrior. The poet describes Atiyamāṉ's dual nature: his extreme generosity and gentleness towards his friends and the needy, contrasted with his fierce, destructive power in times of war. She uses a vivid home-based simile, comparing him to a fire-striking stick (ஞெலிகோல்) tucked quietly in the thatched eaves (இல்லிறை) of a house. Just as the stick remains cold and harmless until struck, Atiyamāṉ remains peaceful and unassuming among simple folk (மடவர்). However, when provoked or when the time for battle arrives, he bursts forth like a raging, spark-spitting fire (கனைஎரி) to destroy his enemies. Key words include 'ஞெலிகோல்' (fire-striking stick) and 'கனைஎரி' (intense fire), which beautifully capture his latent power and sudden, fierce manifestation.",
